A||||4||Phantom Rage||Leaking Green Stuff (HELPPPPPPPPPPPPP)
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||09-01-99||10:37 AM||||Coolant, coolant, coolant, everywhere, so much coolant, I can't bear.  The floor mat on the passengers side is soaked.  I was told it was the heater core.  I looked into the Chilton's and Haynes manual.  It looked pretty easy in the Chilton's, the Haynes just a little more complicated.  From past experience I have found these manuals tend to leave out just a little tip, vital to the repair.  How hard is it to replace, and does any one happen to have any of those vital tips? P.S. My A/C(cool) works fine, but no heat.  Not really sure if the heater core is the culprit, but kinda makes sense.                   <br>                        Thx for any comments
Z||000001||BENGAL4||09-01-99||11:26 AM||||It looks like it is indeed your heater core. Just replaced mine a few months ago and it's not a hard job. One trick I learned is to take out the dash speaker just over the top of the housing. This makes getting to the top right bolts on the housing easier. When you are finished, check the hot to cold lever on the heater to make sure it is not binding. I didn't and I had to diassemble and clear it. Good luck. 
Z||000002||88 Fiero||09-01-99||12:15 PM||||It's the heater core alright....and like Bengal4 said it's not hard to replace it...use the haynes book instead of chilton...chilton is the one that leaves alot of things when it comes to repairs....
Z||000003||Phantom Rage||09-01-99||08:49 PM||||Hey guys or girls, thx for the replys.  I feel a whole lot more confident now about the whole thing.  I will try to get it done this weekend, once I catch up with some of my homework. <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15> 
Z||000004||DJRice||09-02-99||07:00 AM||||dont forget about the quick fix, if you dont want to be bothered with a doing the whole job now.  You can just connect the two heater hoses together with a piece of pipe and make sure you clamp them securely.  <p>That will reduce your down time while you locate a core.  I had to order mine....about $45 as I recall.
